The distance–time graph shows a car travelling at constant speed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.5,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$d$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/50,2/100,3/150,4/200,5/250} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,0) -- (2.5,3.6);
\fill (2.5,3.6) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (2.5,3.6) {$(2.5,180)$};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2.75) {Distance (km)};
\node[below] at (2.7,-0.9) {Time (h)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the average speed of the car?

The graph shows a journey where a driver travels $90\text{ km}$ in $1.5\text{ hours}$, stops for $0.5\text{ hours}$, and travels another $60\text{ km}$ in $1\text{ hour}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (4.5,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$d$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/30,2/60,3/90,4/120,5/150} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,0) -- (1.5,3.0) -- (2.0,3.0) -- (3.0,5.0);
\fill (0,0) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (1.5,3.0) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (2.0,3.0) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (3.0,5.0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2.75) {Distance (km)};
\node[below] at (2.2,-0.9) {Time (h)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the overall average speed for the entire $3\text{-hour}$ trip?
